The ClientID-vs-ClientNumber call-out in the hint is high-value: it covers the second most common cause of this failure (operator confusing the two identifiers, which is a documented Lacerte SDK gotcha already called out elsewhere in the codebase). Also bake a one-line test into ClientsToolsTests proving the not-found envelope carries `hint` and the found envelope does not (so future refactors don't strip it). Optionally apply the same pattern to `LacerteSubclientRead` for the rows.Count==0 + unknown-client case — but tread carefully there: zero subclients is legitimately empty for many clients (single filer with no dependents), so the hint should only fire when the parent ClientNumber itself doesn't exist; otherwise an empty subclient list is informational, not an error. Defer Option 1 (new SyntheticStatusCodes.ClientNotFound 9016) to v0.2 alongside the planned legacy-field removal — bundling the breaking shape changes is cleaner than dripping them out.
